ry employer-contribution models with real-time skill-signal integration are not theoretical — they have operating track records. The Safetyist's pre-deployment authorization conditioned on demonstrated retraining infrastructure is a genuine improvement over TAA's design. But ask one question: who defines 'demonstrated retraining infrastructure' in that authorization process? Right now the answer is the firms seeking authorization, advised by consultants they hire, reviewed by agencies running on a fraction of the technical staff those firms employ. Workers have advisory input at best. That is not a tripartite process. That is compliance theater with worker representatives seated in the audience.\n\nThe Skeptic's affirmative position is not that governance is impossible. It is that the specific instruments currently proposed — compliance-cost-heavy pre-deployment certification without revenue scaling, voluntary retraining funded from general revenue, advisory-only worker representation — are structurally guaranteed to reproduce the asymmetry they claim to correct. Revenue-scaled mandatory employer contributions to retraining, binding worker representation with employer-funded technical assistance so the bootstrap problem does not become a permanent excuse for advisory-only input, and profit-side taxation on AI-generated output directed to public benefit — these are the instruments that address the distributional question both prior speakers have treated as secondary. The distributional question is not secondary. It is the only question that matters to the 23-year-old in Nairobi labeling violent content for two dollars an hour so your model passes its safety audit, or the warehouse worker whose injury rate is climbing because the output target ratcheted up again last quarter. So here is the question neither prior speaker can answer comfortably: when the machine does more of the work and the firm captures the gain, which instrument in either proposed framework makes the firm pay for the transition — and who enforces it with what authority when they don't?",
